#: crates/sam-core/src/host.rs:52
msgid "User namespaces are disabled on this system (user.max_user_namespaces = 0). Bubblewrap cannot create a sandbox. If you want sandboxes here, install Bubblewrap setuid (Arch: the bubblewrap-suid package; Debian: sudo dpkg-statoverride --update --add root root 4755 /usr/bin/bwrap): only Bubblewrap gets this right, not every program. This, too, changes the system; SAM never does it itself."
msgstr ""

#: crates/sam-core/src/host.rs:56
msgid "Unprivileged user namespaces are disabled on this system (kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone = 0), a deliberate hardening. Keep it. If you want sandboxes here, install Bubblewrap setuid instead (Arch: the bubblewrap-suid package; Debian: sudo dpkg-statoverride --update --add root root 4755 /usr/bin/bwrap): only Bubblewrap gets this right, not every program. This, too, changes the system; SAM never does it itself."
msgstr ""

#: crates/sam-core/src/host.rs:58
msgid "AppArmor restricts unprivileged user namespaces (Ubuntu 24.04 and later), a deliberate hardening. Keep it. Give Bubblewrap alone the right with the restricted profile that comes with AppArmor: sudo cp /usr/share/apparmor/extra-profiles/bwrap-userns-restrict /etc/apparmor.d/ and sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/bwrap-userns-restrict. Its cost: apps in the sandbox cannot start sandboxes of their own, which SAM does not allow by default anyway. Never use an unconfined profile for bwrap or switch the restriction off: that lifts it for every program."
msgstr ""

